;; BIND zone file for aldev.tools -> GitHub Pages (aldevtools/aldev.tools)
;;
;; Import in Cloudflare:  DNS > Records > Import and Export > Import
;;
;; LEAVE "Proxy imported DNS records" UNCHECKED.
;; GitHub has to reach the domain directly to issue the TLS certificate. If the
;; records are proxied (orange cloud) before that happens, certificate issuance
;; fails and the site serves an HTTPS error. Once https://aldev.tools loads with
;; a valid certificate you can turn the proxy on afterwards if you want it.
;;
;; TTL 1 means "Automatic" in Cloudflare.
;;
;; Addresses verified 2026-09-09 by resolving aldevtools.github.io, not quoted
;; from documentation. If GitHub ever changes them, an ALIAS/CNAME at the apex
;; (see the bottom of this file) follows automatically and these do not.

;; --- apex: GitHub Pages IPv4 ---
aldev.tools.	1	IN	A	185.199.108.153
aldev.tools.	1	IN	A	185.199.109.153
aldev.tools.	1	IN	A	185.199.110.153
aldev.tools.	1	IN	A	185.199.111.153

;; --- apex: GitHub Pages IPv6 ---
aldev.tools.	1	IN	AAAA	2606:50c0:8000::153
aldev.tools.	1	IN	AAAA	2606:50c0:8001::153
aldev.tools.	1	IN	AAAA	2606:50c0:8002::153
aldev.tools.	1	IN	AAAA	2606:50c0:8003::153

;; --- www -> apex ---
www.aldev.tools.	1	IN	CNAME	aldevtools.github.io.

;; --- alternative to the eight records above ---
;; Cloudflare flattens CNAMEs at the apex, so this single record works too and
;; keeps following GitHub if their addresses change. Use EITHER this line OR the
;; A/AAAA records above, never both:
;;
;; aldev.tools.	1	IN	CNAME	aldevtools.github.io.
